  "note": "Six candidates were nominated for each ward, so there was no contest. The Frontier Sentinel gives the new council as twelve Nationalists, eight of them of the Catholic Labour Union, and six Unionists, the same balance as the old council. Occupations printed in the source are not recorded. The paper calls all six \"Catholics\", the last two members of the Catholic Labour Union; the Frontier Sentinel lists the other four as Nationalists and prints Magee as George M'Kee."
